{"_id":"6925a6527c7d1fa20e7692c7","roadmapSlug":"elasticsearch","nodeId":"SmaMEuknItGuLiBv9PwIk","description":"# ID Query\n\nAn ID query retrieves documents from an index based on their unique identifier. It's a simple and efficient way to fetch specific documents when you already know their IDs. This query directly accesses the document using its `_id` field.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"IDs","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/query-dsl/query-dsl-ids-query","_id":"69284397467651eddb61afb9"},{"type":"official","title":"Get a document by its ID","url":"https://www.elastic.co/docs/api/doc/elasticsearch/operation/operation-get","_id":"69284397467651eddb61afba"},{"type":"article","title":"Elasticsearch ids query","url":"http://opster.com/guides/elasticsearch/search-apis/elasticsearch-ids-query/","_id":"69284397467651eddb61afbb"},{"type":"article","title":"Stop using the _id field in Elasticsearch","url":"https://luis-sena.medium.com/stop-using-the-id-field-in-elasticsearch-6fb650d1fbae","_id":"69284397467651eddb61afbc"}],"createdAt":"2025-11-25T12:51:30.302Z","updatedAt":"2025-11-27T12:27:03.094Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/elasticsearch/content/SmaMEuknItGuLiBv9PwIk.md"}